Typical for me: Expert in daggers and bows, basic in broadsword or a
melee weapon, maybe skilled in divinations.

> ** Save arrows for tougher foes and Floating Eyes and skill up
> daggers?

My routine: arrows until they run out and daggers are collected, throw
daggers until the quest is over, invoke the Longbow a few times and
cancel/bless/enchant the big stack of 200 arrows that one should have
easily collected by now and use those until the end of the game.  But
don't worry about what you'll be doing post-Quest, get there first.

> ** Balance arrows and daggers?

"Balance"?  Don't know what you mean, but don't overthink it; just
kill everything that is trying to kill you and probably a few more
besides that.  There are plenty of skill slots for both of those
weapons.
>
> * How hard should I be working to ID potions and scrolls before XL 10?
depends on your patience and spoilage level.  For me it's trivial, I
even understand my own short-hand: "a potion named mu20-" is murky
with a typo and a confirmed price of 200 Zm.  I price id everything
before I waste my id scrolls on the easy ones.  Scrolls of ID, light,
EW, EA, RC are all easy to determine with price and then I use my id
scrolls on the 300 Zm ones.

> ** Only price ID Identify and only use them for identify?
> ** Read any uncursed scroll if you are confused?

No, that's wasteful and hazardous.  Just price id and save them.

> ** Drink any potion you find on the first 3 levels since you probably
> won't die?

No, I save them just in case I happened to find Gain Level or Gain
ability since I will use the former to bring me from XL 13 to 14 and I
like to bless the latter.

